   "text": {
    "L1": "A line of symmetry divides a figure into two mirror-image halves.",
    "L2": "Fold on the line: every point must match its mirror point at the same distance.",
    "L3": "Here is a rectangle. Its vertical and horizontal middle lines make matching halves.",
    "L4": "A diagonal also makes two equal-area triangles, but equal area is not enough.",
    "L5": "The diagonal is not a symmetry line because the folded corners do not match exactly.",
    "L6": "Lines of symmetry can be vertical, horizontal, or slanting. H has two: one vertical and one horizontal.",
    "L7": "A quick test is to fold along the line and check whether the halves match point for point.",
    "L8": "Now choose the number of symmetry lines in a rectangle that is not a square."
   },
